1.10.0: weave calibrated against reality, motion-scale knob

Field report: on real, steady 720p footage the gate weave was
practically unobservable - the noise driver rarely reaches nominal
amplitude, and encoding smooths the remainder. Weave and flicker
defaults roughly double (super8 0.0040->0.0085, autochrome
0.0060->0.0110, polavision 0.0045->0.0080, technicolor stays
watchmaker-steady at 0.0028), and calibration moves to the terminal:
pj_render gains motion_scale, superjuice --motion-scale, and super8ify
MOTION= - scaling weave and flicker together, grain untouched, 0 for
tripod-locked, 2 for a worn projector. Core and movie suites assert
the scale changes the render.
